# toolchain.env — ⛔ THE ONE TOOLCHAIN MANIFEST: the exact version of every tool a CI job or a local gate runs
# (kb/Work PB4007; ToolchainManifestDriftTests; DESIGN-test-build-ci.md §1.4).
#
# The owner, 2026-10-28: "CI tooling should match local tooling versions - always", then "CI and local should always be
# using the latest version". So CI and every local host run the version named here, and each version here is that
# tool's latest stable release. This is the only place a version is written:
#   * CI: every job's first step after its checkout is ./.github/actions/setup-toolchain, which installs these versions
#     (Python through actions/setup-python, everything else through scripts/install-tool.sh) and fails unless each tool
#     on PATH reports its version here (`python scripts/toolchain.py check --scope ci`). The runner images are pinned to
#     the two labels below, and the workflow's `runs-on:` lines must name them.
#   * The Windows dev box: winget installs the tools (Python through the Python Install Manager); the gate refuses to
#     run, NOT RUN [toolchain], while a tool it runs reports another version (`toolchain.py check --scope gate`), and the
#     SessionStart readiness check (scripts/hooks/tooling_check.py) prints the same comparison for every tool.
#   * WSL (scripts/wsl/setup-wsl.sh) and the cloud image (scripts/cloud/setup-env.sh) install from this file.
#   * scripts/python-resolve.sh and .ps1 accept only an interpreter of exactly PYTHON_VERSION.
# The cloud setup runs before the repository is cloned, so it carries a copy of the block between the `toolchain`
# markers, and ToolchainManifestDriftTests holds the two copies byte-identical.
#
# KEEPING IT AT THE LATEST: `python scripts/toolchain.py latest` asks each publisher for its newest stable release and
# exits 1 naming every tool this file is behind on; the scheduled workflow .github/workflows/toolchain-freshness.yml runs
# it every day, so a release this file lacks is a red scheduled run, never silence. `python scripts/toolchain.py bump`
# then moves this file and its cloud copy forward, in a change of its own that carries the hosts' update (winget on the
# Windows box, scripts/wsl/setup-wsl.sh in WSL, the cloud environment's setup script pasted again) and is gated and
# landed like any other: CI and the hosts move to the new version together.
#
# Two values are not installed by this repository, and each says why:
#   * GIT_LINUX_VERSION and GIT_WINDOWS_VERSION: actions/checkout runs the runner image's git before any file of the
#     repository exists, and no publisher ships a Linux git of a chosen version, so CI runs each image's git and these
#     name it (git's own release, without Git for Windows' `.windows.N` packaging suffix): `toolchain.py latest` reads
#     each from its image's readme, and each host installs that release (Git for Windows on the Windows dev box, the
#     git-core PPA in WSL). One value per image, because GitHub rolls the two images on different weeks. A CI job on an
#     image whose git moved warns and runs; the daily toolchain-freshness run is red on it (`check --scope image`) until
#     `toolchain.py bump` follows it, so a moved image never stops a landing and is never silent.
#   * SEMGREP_PYTHON_VERSION: semgrep (scripts/semgrep/verify.py; local only, CI runs none) cannot run on Python 3.15
#     yet: semgrep 1.18x pins ruamel.yaml.clib 0.2.15, which has no cp315 wheel and does not build. It runs as a uv tool
#     on this older uv-managed CPython (`uv tool install semgrep==<SEMGREP_VERSION> --python <SEMGREP_PYTHON_VERSION>
#     --managed-python`), apart from the project interpreter. Drop the line, and install semgrep on PYTHON_VERSION, once
#     upstream ships a cp315 wheel.
#
# >>> toolchain (kept byte-identical in toolchain.env and scripts/cloud/setup-env.sh)
DOTNET_SDK_VERSION=10.0.403
PYTHON_VERSION=3.15.2
JDK_VERSION=27.0.1
PWSH_VERSION=7.6.9
GIT_LINUX_VERSION=2.56.0
GIT_WINDOWS_VERSION=2.56.0
GH_VERSION=2.103.3
JQ_VERSION=1.8.2
UV_VERSION=0.13.6
SEMGREP_VERSION=1.183.0
SEMGREP_PYTHON_VERSION=3.14.10
CI_LINUX_IMAGE=ubuntu-26.04
CI_WINDOWS_IMAGE=windows-2025-vs2026
# <<< toolchain
